The difficulty with this method is the severe cross terms as indicated by the existence of negative power for some frequency ranges. Although this shortcoming can
be eliminated by using the Kernel method (see, for example, Cohen 1995), the result
is, then, basically that of a windowed Fourier analysis; therefore, it suffers all the limitations of the Fourier analysis. An extension of this method has been made by Yen
(1994), who used the Wigner–Ville distribution to define wave packets that reduce


