Figure 53. The Hilbert spectrum for the wave data at station 5. Other than the two locations
of phase jumps, the frequency of the wave train stays at a very narrow range of intrawave
modulation, and could be considered as having gradual and continuous frequency changes. But
at the phase jump locations, the frequency of the wave train undergoes so much change as to
make the assumption of a gradual and continuous function invalid.


Figure 54. Comparison of the marginal spectrum and the Fourier spectrum at station 5. ( _a_ ) The
marginal spectrum for station 5 showing a relative wide distribution of frequency, and a slight
